# Emergency braking (docs/emergency_stop.md) on the burn-in axis (10 mm a
# revolution; 1 rad = 1.59 mm). hv0.sim_dist, zeroed at the failure, is how
# far the axis went.
# The F4 stops while the drive is enabled at standstill: the F3 brakes
# (nothing to do), ends after its 0.1 s low-current check, and switches off.
@args --drive ../hwtest/burnin/ECMA-C30604FS/stmbl.conf
@timeout 120
lcnc 0 0
run 0.5
lcnc 1 0
run 1.5
run 0.5
hv0.sim_dist = 0
hv0.sim_f4_dead = 1
run 0.01
hv0.sim_f3_brake
run 0.3
hv0.sim_f3_brake
hv0.sim_dist
@expect hv0.sim_f3_brake[1] == 1
@expect hv0.sim_f3_brake[2] == 0
@expect hv0.sim_dist ~ 0 0.01
